course: dictionary
lesson: 8139
title: Thinking before you repost
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To repost means to post something online again, especially something someone else posted first. The prefix re- means again. «Posting someone's art without their name takes away their credit.» The art was made by one person, so reposting it without their name hides who made it.
explain: Repost can also be a noun: a repost is a post that has been shared again. The verb changes its form: repost, reposts, reposted, reposting. «Repost a video» means share a video again. «Repost without permission» means share it again without asking the person who made it.
explain: Before you repost, stop and ask three questions: Is it true? Whose is it? Could it hurt someone? A rumour passed on again can spread lies quickly, and a photo of someone shared again can hurt them, even if you meant it as a joke.
fact: Repost is a verb (to repost) and a noun (a repost).
fact: «Repost» means to post something online again, especially something someone else posted.
fact: «Repost without permission» means sharing something again without asking the person who made it.
fact: Artists often sign their work, and many sites let people report reposts that break the rules.
fact: Reposting a rumour or someone's photo can spread lies or hurt someone, so think before you share.
exercise: What does «repost» mean? | To take a photo of your screen | To delete a post for ever | To send a letter by post | *To post something online again, especially something someone else posted
exercise: Which phrase means sharing something again without asking the owner first? | take away their credit | repost a video | *repost without permission | sign their work
exercise: Ayaan's friend reposts a rumour he has not checked. Why is this risky? | It can spread lies quickly to many people | It makes the rumour true | *It can spread lies quickly to many people, and some people may be hurt by it | It turns the rumour into a poem
test: In «I will repost it tomorrow», what kind of word is repost? | *Verb | Noun | Adverb | Adjective
test: «Posting someone's art without their name takes away their credit.» Why is this a problem? | *Their work is shared without showing who made it | It makes the art cheaper | Art is always free to copy | The art turns into a letter
exam: Which step should you take before you repost someone's photo? | Share it at once so it is not forgotten | *Ask whether it is true and whether it could hurt them | Post it without a name so no one knows who sent it | Add more filters so it looks better
